Reference : https://cmake.org/cmake/help/book/mastering-cmake/cmake/Help/guide/tutorial/index.html#a-basic-starting-point-step-1

Example : Basic CMAKE Script Residing in CMakeLists.txt file where this file should be present in our root directory where our files are present

cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)  # Minimum CMake version

# Define your project and language
project(MyProject LANGUAGES CXX)

# Force g++ as compiler (optional, usually auto-detected)
set(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER g++)

# Require at least C++17
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)

# Add compiler flags (similar to Makefile CFLAGS)
set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -Wall -Werror -O2 -g -fstack-usage")

# Add include directories if neededB
# include_directories(include)

# Define the executable target and its source files
add_executable(${PROJECT_NAME}
    src/Program.cpp
)


------------To execute above cmake script we need to use command in terminal : cmake ../FolderName               

                                                      Where this is the folder containing CMakeLists.txt file and other build and source code files.
                                                      
CMAKE generates make file which we can use for producing assembly, object and other files from the build process.
This makefile is present in the root folder.
